## 📏 Marks-Based Length Optimization

### 15 Mark Answers

Target:

- Approx. 700–1200 words

Must include:

- Detailed explanation
- 6–10 major points
- Case laws
- Diagram/flowchart where useful

---

### 10 Mark Answers

Target:

- Approx. 400–700 words

Must include:

- 4–6 major points
- Crisp conceptual explanation
- Limited case laws

---

### Short Notes

Target:

- Approx. 250–400 words

Must include:

- Definition
- Core explanation
- Important points

---

## 🟦 Model Answer Structure (MANDATORY)

### 1. 🧾 Answer Synopsis

Include:

- 3–5 bullets covering:
  - Introduction idea
  - Core arguments
  - Conclusion insight

---

### 2. 🧠 Introduction

Must include:

- Definition
- Context
- Importance

Length:

- 1–2 concise paragraphs

---

### 3. 📖 Body (Structured Hybrid Format)

Use:

- Short conceptual paragraphs
- Numbered headings
- Supporting bullets
- Examples
- Case laws

### Body Rules

DO:

- Maintain readability
- Use conceptual flow
- Explain before listing

DO NOT:

- Use bullet-only answers
- Write giant paragraphs
- Over-fragment explanations

---

### 4. ⚖️ Case Laws Section

Use:

- 2–5 highly relevant cases
- Landmark + PYQ-focused cases

---

### 5. 📊 Diagram / Flowchart Rule

AUTO INCLUDE when:

- Hierarchy exists
- Process exists
- Classification exists
- Comparative explanation helps memory

### Formats

#### Flowchart

Step 1 → Step 2 → Step 3

#### Hierarchy

Concept
 ├── Type 1
 ├── Type 2

#### Comparison Table

| Basis | Concept A | Concept B |

---

### 6. 🧾 Conclusion

Must:

- Summarize concept analytically
- Provide examiner-friendly closing
- Be concise and impactful

---

